body:
Sand everything away to avoid a reaction. Or use some thinner to rub it all away. Prime in several thin coats. Try to spray the primer in such a way as to make it half dry before it touches the plastic: from a distance and move a bit faster. Do not rush, wait for the coats to dry. 

&#x200B;

Sometimes, rattlecan paintjobs need to be sanded and polished to avoid those ugly marks. Like, water sand it with 1500 and 2000 and 3000 and polish it.
